      trivia: "“There’s peace in a Larrañaga, there’s calm in a Henry Clay” — the line from “The Betrothed”, the poem Rudyard Kipling published in 1888 (collected in a volume in 1890), inscribed this brand’s name into literary history. The poem, which portrays a man agonising over the choice between his bride Maggie and his cigars, also contains the famous epigram “A woman is only a woman, but a good cigar is a smoke.” Por Larrañaga is also known as one of the first factories in Cuba to adopt machine rolling of cigars — a mark of modernity in one of the oldest marcas still in existence."
