      trivia: "Vegueros is that rarity among current Habanos: a brand sold in bright metal tins rather than wooden boxes. Its name is the Spanish for “tobacco farmers” — a singular pedigree crowned not with a famous factory or a personal name but with the fields and the farmers themselves. Its maker, the Francisco Donatién factory, occupies an 1868 building (said by some accounts to have been a prison) converted in 1961, and doubles as a tourist attraction open to visitors. At the total rebrand of 2013 it was reported to be “out in April”, yet actual sales slipped to mid-2014, earning the specialist-press headline “Vegueros, At Last”. With the 2023 Centrogordos it adopted the new “centro gordo” vitola — a value brand that has become a proving ground for new dimensions."
